# SRG-APP-000111-AU-000150  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to perform analysis of log
# records across multiple devices and hosts in the enclave that can be
# reviewed by authorized individuals.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000111-AU-000150
group:           V-206455
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000154
control_rev5:    AU-6

contribution:    Splunk's search layer analyzes records from every host and device together
                 because they share one index set, and role configuration determines which
                 of those indexes an authorized reviewer may search.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.

check:           authorize.conf [] srchIndexesAllowed non_empty

external:        Which individuals are authorized to review the analysis, and their
                 assignment to a Splunk role, is an organizational and directory service
                 matter.

citation:        OVER-REACH, and one mislabeled dependency. Removed savedsearches.conf
                 [<stanza name>] search non_empty: the shipped savedsearches.conf declares
                 "search =" empty, so the condition fails a stock instance, and saved
                 searches are not required for cross-host analysis - the search layer
                 analyzes the whole index set on demand. Separately, distsearch.conf
                 [distributedSearch] servers was listed as an external dependency: it is
                 Splunk configuration, which the application can reach, so that label is
                 wrong. It is not promoted to a condition either, because an
                 indexer-cluster search head receives its peer list from the cluster
                 manager rather than from distsearch.conf, so a mandatory non_empty would
                 falsely fail that topology; the assessor reads whichever of the two
                 applies.
finding:         No role is permitted to search the indexes holding the aggregated records
                 (srchIndexesAllowed is unset), so cross-host analysis cannot be reviewed
                 by the authorized individuals.
